<%# A slice cut off a branch with a bind-rune burned into it, in its own local
    frame: the cord is tied at 0,0 and the disc hangs out and below. `ox` is how
    far out, `top` is where the wood starts — under the cord for something
    hanging, and centred on the spot for something lying down, which is the
    only difference between the two.

    The disc is drawn twice. A token is small enough that a silhouette alone
    disappears against the night and a bright shape alone disappears against
    the moon, so it gets a dark contour under a pale face and reads on either —
    which is the same thing the names do with a bevel and a halo. %>
<g opacity="<%= offering[:glare] %>">
  <path class="offering__halo" d="<%= offering[:disc] %>"/>
  <path class="offering__disc" d="<%= offering[:disc] %>"/>
  <path class="offering__rune" d="<%= offering[:marks] %>"/>
</g>
